GLtron - Installation from source

The maintained instructions for Linux, Windows, and macOS are in BUILDING.md.

Linux quick build from a Git checkout:

  ./autogen.sh
  ./configure --enable-localdata
  make
  ./gltron

The --enable-localdata option runs against the resources in the checkout. For
a system installation, configure without that option, then run:

  make
  sudo make install

The default data directory is /usr/local/share/gltron. User preferences are
stored in $HOME/.gltronrc and screenshots in $HOME.

Run "./gltron -h" for runtime options. The "-s" option disables sound.
